WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.461
On most blockchains,

00:00:01.461 --> 00:00:03.339
anyone who knows an address can read its

00:00:03.339 --> 00:00:05.600
balance and every amount it paid.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.800
On Aztec, a token can have two balances.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.678
Nulo handles both for you.

00:00:10.678 --> 00:00:12.070
Your private balance:

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.670
only you can see it.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:14.991
Your public balance:

00:00:14.991 --> 00:00:16.174
anyone can see it,

00:00:16.174 --> 00:00:18.000
like a balance on Ethereum.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.252
Your private balance is a

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.609
set of encrypted notes,

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:22.696
like cash in sealed envelopes.

00:00:22.696 --> 00:00:24.261
The network keeps a fingerprint

00:00:24.261 --> 00:00:25.177
of each note,

00:00:25.177 --> 00:00:28.043
and a sealed copy only its owner can open.

00:00:28.043 --> 00:00:30.617
Say you pay 3.50 from a note worth 5.

00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:33.887
Nulo spends that note and makes new ones:

00:00:33.887 --> 00:00:35.696
3.50 for the person you pay,

00:00:35.696 --> 00:00:37.783
and 1.50 change for you.

00:00:37.783 --> 00:00:39.000
In a private payment,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.330
the record shows that something was spent.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.070
It does not show which note,

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.374
or how much.

00:00:44.374 --> 00:00:45.696
Moving money to your public

00:00:45.696 --> 00:00:46.994
balance is your choice,

00:00:46.994 --> 00:00:49.174
and the public side records the amount.

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:50.774
Nulo labels each balance,

00:00:50.774 --> 00:00:52.652
so you always know which is which.
